                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more Proustian"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5b1ad9e0-c880-49e9-ba31-18680d2845a4",
                        "entry_id": "6c950ba3-e194-3d3d-aeff-cf3cd70ef33f",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Proustian"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fb1a205-df28-359d-accf-6040ba6efe68",
                        "entry_id": "6c950ba3-e194-3d3d-aeff-cf3cd70ef33f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, pertaining to, or reminiscent of Marcel Proust (1871–1922), French novelist, or his works."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db5eb7a3-105a-43c4-aff7-d0ccd5bb715c",
                                "sense_id": "7fb1a205-df28-359d-accf-6040ba6efe68",
                                "text": "The character played by French female lead Lea Seydoux is even called Madeleine Swann, a name whose Proustian double resonance can only be deliberate."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa3592ba-cca9-371c-ac32-ede77ce44ffb",
                        "entry_id": "6c950ba3-e194-3d3d-aeff-cf3cd70ef33f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Derived from personal memory, as it often happens in the works of Proust (for example, in the experience of the madeleine)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59295279-1ddd-49ec-b591-443042a825d6",
                                "sense_id": "fa3592ba-cca9-371c-ac32-ede77ce44ffb",
                                "text": "D'Costa's poems so far published also reverberate with an awareness of the past, and a gently Proustian pleasure, as in the elegiac “In Memorandum”."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5b710f55-78d3-42ba-aca5-8a7bf7331ed4",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c950ba3-e194-3d3d-aeff-cf3cd70ef33f",
                        "source_sense_description": "reminiscent of Marcel Proust or his works",
                        "target_lang_word": "proustovský",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a826fa8b-5a4a-4f9d-9474-36217a0962e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c950ba3-e194-3d3d-aeff-cf3cd70ef33f",
                        "source_sense_description": "reminiscent of Marcel Proust or his works",
                        "target_lang_word": "proustien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "proustien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5938e9f7-b9e6-3973-bc20-d5df0652fd23",
                                        "entry_id": "814b936e-1377-3bb5-b6b9-e9de88a40ba6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui appartient à l’écrivain Marcel Proust ou à son œuvre, qui rappelle la société mondaine de la fin du XIXᵉ siècle et du début du XXᵉ telle que cet auteur l’a évoquée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe1e2db4-f474-47c4-ba57-7309b495b79c",
                                                "sense_id": "5938e9f7-b9e6-3973-bc20-d5df0652fd23",
                                                "text": "« J’ai une âme de concierge proustienne », disait-elle complaisamment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04acefc4-304d-4f8f-aeb7-0cce90cff515",
                                                "sense_id": "5938e9f7-b9e6-3973-bc20-d5df0652fd23",
                                                "text": "Si, en fonction du théorème proustien, je regarde ma personnalité à travers une image dessinée par les autres, alors c’est ce trait qui est dominant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80768a18-6ae0-4a2e-8273-e8322d15c525",
                                                "sense_id": "5938e9f7-b9e6-3973-bc20-d5df0652fd23",
                                                "text": "[Emil] Cioran semble bien respecter la consigne proustienne : « le devoir et la tâche d’un écrivain sont ceux d’un traducteur » et il se trouve souvent dans l’impossibilité d’écrire, tout comme il se tourmente dans l’impossibilité de tout traduire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57b592ba-ede5-4dd3-9df6-ead07d299080",
                                                "sense_id": "5938e9f7-b9e6-3973-bc20-d5df0652fd23",
                                                "text": "À Courcelle, le petit poirier se dresse tel un archange proustien et la haie basse de noisetiers, le long de la route, est vêtue de feuilles neuves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
